## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/edgedetectnormal.html
- Summary (EN): Detects crease lines of varying width by comparing the input vector, typically a surface normal, at each pixel with its neighbours using ray differentials.
- Résumé (FR) : Trace les lignes de pli d'épaisseur variable en comparant les normales de chaque pixel à celles de ses voisins.

- Inputs meaning: ["normal: normal input processed for crease-line detection", "thickness: optional input that multiplies Thickness Scale rather than replacing it"]

- Key parameters: ["Thickness Scale: kernel radius in pixels; a multiplier when thickness is connected", "Edge Spread: multiplies the Gaussian weight spread", "Blur: blurs the input before detection", "Normal Tolerance: minimum dot product between a pixel normal and its neighbours' normals for them to count as part of the line", "Min Probe Radius: minimum search radius for probe pixels"]

- Caveats: ["The page gives no default values, performance notes or examples.", "The page does not explain how Normal Tolerance interacts with the other parameters; tuning may need experiments."]

